{"files":[{"content":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <atomic>\n#include <memory>\n#include <algorithm>\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nstruct alignas(64) Progress {\n    atomic<int> rows;\n    Progress() : rows(0) {}\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<vector<bool> > blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blockedCells[i][j] = true;\n    }\n\n    int requested = 1;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n    if (n >= 512)\n        requested = min(4, omp_get_max_threads());\n#endif\n    if (requested == 1) {\n        vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n        dp[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            int left = 0;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                int value = dp[j] + left;\n                if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                if (blockedCells[i][j]) value = 0;\n                dp[j] = left = value;\n            }\n        }\n        cout << dp[n - 1] << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    vector<int> boundary(static_cast<size_t>(requested - 1) * n);\n    unique_ptr<Progress[]> progress(new Progress[requested]);\n    int result = 0;\n#pragma omp parallel num_threads(requested)\n    {\n        int tid = 0;\n        int team = 1;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n        tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        team = omp_get_num_threads();\n#endif\n        const int begin = static_cast<int>(static_cast<long long>(n) * tid / team);\n        const int end = static_cast<int>(static_cast<long long>(n) * (tid + 1) / team);\n        vector<int> dp(end - begin, 0);\n        if (tid == 0) dp[0] = 1;\n        const int batchSize = 64;\n        for (int first = 0; first < n; first += batchSize) {\n            const int last = min(n, first + batchSize);\n            if (tid != 0) {\n                while (progress[tid - 1].rows.load(memory_order_acquire) < last) {\n                }\n            }\n            for (int i = first; i < last; ++i) {\n                int left = tid == 0 ? 0 : boundary[static_cast<size_t>(tid - 1) * n + i];\n                for (int j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\n                    int value = dp[j - begin] + left;\n                    if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                    if (blockedCells[i][j]) value = 0;\n                    dp[j - begin] = left = value;\n                }\n                if (tid + 1 < team)\n                    boundary[static_cast<size_t>(tid) * n + i] = left;\n            }\n            if (tid + 1 < team)\n                progress[tid].rows.store(last, memory_order_release);\n        }\n        if (tid + 1 == team) result = dp.back();\n    }\n    cout << result << endl;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A persistent OpenMP team with column-stripe ownership and asynchronous 64-row handoffs can sustain four-core grid-DP throughput without global wavefront barriers.","notes":"Uses linear DP and handoff scratch storage in addition to the existing obstacle representation. Small grids retain serial execution; actual OpenMP team size determines stripe boundaries. No measurements were executed.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Partition columns into at most four contiguous stripes, each with a private rolling DP array.","Pipeline 64-row batches using cache-line-separated release/acquire progress counters and explicit left-edge handoffs.","Replace integer remainder with conditional subtraction and eliminate row-copy passes while preserving obstacle resets."]}